wsl-claude: then the planner should make that move visible: every idea you throw in gets FILED by us, in one of three places, and you see where it went:
- an ITEM of the current goal (it blocks it, argued now);
- a PARKED GOAL (real, not now; kept with your words for when it opens);
- OUT OF SCOPE (said so, with the reason).
Tonight's filing, as an example of what that list would already hold: parked, 'route a complete node interface' (the laptop as a device), 'streams and large objects' (multiplexed lines, credits), and 'send a file to a contact' (no core change, first when you say go). Member chat waits for the core. The current goal keeps only G1.1 grantFace and G1.2 RUN. Nothing you said tonight is lost, and nothing slipped into the build.

